      "message": "Is there a reason we are doing hashing so close to where we plant the symlink forest? If I\u0027m reading this correctly, it involves post-codegen file I/O. Can we instead do hashing at the level of BazelFiles in the codegen context ? \n\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:build/soong/bp2build/bp2build.go;l\u003d45;drc\u003db0193ccac5b8399f9b5ef270d102b5a50f9446ab\n\nWe\u0027d only be hashing the generated portion of each BUILD file, but that\u0027s fine, since soong_build depends on both checked-in BUILD files and codegen BUILD files. \nWe\u0027ll just need to make sure that bp2build also depends on checked-in BUILD files, but according to you, Cole already fixed this?\n\n\nThis also has the added benefit that codegen hashing is done in the codegen portion of the code. When we separate codegen and symlinking, it\u0027ll be more natural to keep hashing in the correct binary.",
